    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure stores auxiliary information for decoding, presenting, or otherwise processing the coded stream. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It is typically exported by demuxers and encoders and can be fed to decoders and muxers either in a per packet basis, or as global side data (applying to the entire coded stream).</para>
<para>Global side data is handled as follows:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>During demuxing, it may be exported through <ref refid="structAVCodecParameters_1ad54da9241deabb3601e6e0e8fa832c19" kindref="member">AVStream&apos;s codec parameters</ref>, which can then be passed as input to decoders through the <ref refid="structAVCodecContext_1a0d9375d5c81895b9048644e547b33d32" kindref="member">decoder context&apos;s side data</ref>, for initialization.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For muxing, it can be fed through <ref refid="structAVCodecParameters_1ad54da9241deabb3601e6e0e8fa832c19" kindref="member">AVStream&apos;s codec parameters</ref>, typically the output of encoders through the <ref refid="structAVCodecContext_1a0d9375d5c81895b9048644e547b33d32" kindref="member">encoder context&apos;s side data</ref>, for initialization.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Packet specific side data is handled as follows:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>During demuxing, it may be exported through <ref refid="structAVPacket_1ac55bfef91c33f02704ba76518d0f294c" kindref="member">AVPacket&apos;s side data</ref>, which can then be passed as input to decoders.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For muxing, it can be fed through <ref refid="structAVPacket_1ac55bfef91c33f02704ba76518d0f294c" kindref="member">AVPacket&apos;s</ref> side data", typically the output of encoders.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Different modules may accept or export different types of side data depending on media type and codec. Refer to <ref refid="group__lavc__packet__side__data_1ga9a80bfcacc586b483a973272800edb97" kindref="member">AVPacketSideDataType</ref> for a list of defined types and where they may be found or used. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
